            "id": 12,
            "filename": "icsr-08-fr-form.pdf",
            "mimeType": "application/pdf",
            "processable": true,
            "pdfFlavor": "NON_ENGLISH",
            "detectedLanguage": "fr",
            "pageCount": 1,
            "processed": true,
            "summary": "This document is a report of an adverse effect experienced by a 38-year-old male patient who was treated with Ferbolex, a medication taken orally at a dose of 500 mg twice daily. The treatment period lasted from July 14, 2026, to July 18, 2026. The attending physician, Dr. Lucas Moreau from France, reported that the patient developed a skin rash and significant itching on July 17, 2026, which resolved after the medication was stopped. The report indicates that the adverse reaction was not serious, and there were no notable medical history complications for the patient.\n\nGiven that this document describes a patient's adverse reaction to a medication, it is relevant to a patient-safety review. Adverse effect reports like this help track the safety of medications and identify any potential risks associated with their use. The information is crucial for assessing the safety profile of Ferbolex and ensuring appropriate patient monitoring. The report can also assist in making informed decisions regarding patient care and managing any similar cases in the future. Overall, this document contributes valuable insights into the pharmacovigilance process."
        }
    ],
